# The payload carriers are BINARY despite their extensions. A CRLF conversion
# would rewrite bytes inside a planted EMF record and the handset would get a
# document that no longer transfers pc -- silently, with the file still looking
# like a valid .MHT. w53ca's carrier is a .HTM for the same reason, so the
# extension says nothing about the content.
*.MHT binary
*.mht binary
*.DOC binary
*.doc binary
*.HTM binary
*.htm binary
*.bin binary
*.zip binary

# Everything else is text with LF, which is what the Linux side that runs the
# pushes expects.
*.py  text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# The manifests are STORED VERBATIM, not normalised. Two of them have CRLF
# because they are hand-edited on the Windows side, and `text eol=lf` would
# have git rewrite them the next time it touched the tree -- a phantom
# modification nobody made. Nothing reads these files line-endings-first.
*.json -text
